  "description": "Discontinued. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic BFe.\n\nModel year: 2016\n\nThe 2016 BFe 26 replaced the BFe 26 Classic (see BFe 26 Classic). Its brother was the BFe 275: see the BFe archive, and the current BFe.\n\nThe BFe 26 is the tearaway of the Cotic family: a rowdy, fast, fun machine.\n\n26 definitely ain't dead! The new BFe 26 was the hardnut of the Cotic family. It featured our first update to our classic 26\" wheeled geometry, with the longer reach and slacker head angle developed on the BFe 275, ideal to pair with the short stems and wide bars we've come to love.\n\nThe BFe 26 is for hard riding. You can run a 100mm fork for 4X and dirtjump duties. 120mm or 140mm forks make it a sweet handling trail bike. Or you can plug in a 160mm fork and send it down the Megavalanche. Most BFe 26 builds perform mighty fine as bold-as-brass razz-around play bikes.\n\nThe frame is based around a Reynolds 853 down tube, which allows us to keep massive strength where it matters most whilst keeping weight down. The rest of the frame is our own Fm heat treated double butted cromoly steel, which helps keep strength and value high throughout. No corners are cut: all the usual Cotic features of Ovalform top tube, oversized plug welded seat tube, wishbone stays, cowled dropouts and a taper steerer compatible head tube are present and correct.\n\nYou could build it with those great 26\" parts you still had, or even plug in 27.5\" forks so long as you kept the 26\" wheels in there.\n\nFun with a capital F, Durable with a capital D: Burly Iron.",
